================================================================================
THE BUNDLED AUDIO IS NOT UNDER THIS LICENCE
================================================================================

The MIT terms above cover the source code. The guitar recordings in `public/`
are third-party works under their own licences:

  public/samples/acoustic/    GPL-3.0-or-later
                             FreePats FS Seagull steel-string, from samples by
                             Gary Campion (FlameStudios), 2008.
                             Full text: public/samples/acoustic/GPL.txt
                             Provenance: public/samples/acoustic/SOURCE.txt

  public/samples/classical/   CC0 1.0 (public domain)
                             FreePats Spanish classical guitar.

  public/samples/electric/    CC0 1.0 (public domain)
                             FreePats Electric Guitar FSBS (clean).

The acoustic samples are copyleft. They live in their own directory, are not
linked into the application, and are loaded at runtime like any other static
asset — the ordinary mere-aggregation case, which is why the source code can be
MIT. If you redistribute those files, GPL.txt and SOURCE.txt must travel with
them.

To make this project wholly permissive, delete public/samples/acoustic/ and its
entry in src/lib/audio/samples/index.ts. Nothing else refers to it.

This is a reading of the licences, not legal advice.
